{%- comment -%}
  Organization JSON-LD. Site-wide, in <head>, once.

  Declares MamaJoy as an entity separate from any one page — the raw
  material for a brand SERP feature or a knowledge panel, neither of which
  Google can build from a Product node alone.

  Every property here is a fact that is already published somewhere a
  shopper can see, which is the test each one has to pass:

    email        the branded support address, also shown in the footer and
                 on /pages/support.
    telephone    the number printed under "Talk to us" on /pages/about and
                 "Contact us" on /pages/support, with the same hours. It is
                 a public support line, not the billing contact it was
                 mistaken for when this file first went in.
    founder      a name, and only a name. No jobTitle beyond "Founder", no
                 bio, no credentials, no award — none of that is
                 established anywhere, and Person is exactly the node where
                 inventing it would be most damaging.

  Still deliberately absent: logo (the header is a text wordmark; there is
  no logo asset to point at, and Google requires a real image) and sameAs
  (no verified social profiles exist yet). Both are a one-line addition the
  day they do. Absent is safer than wrong.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign brand = settings.brand_name | default: shop.name -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": {{ brand | json }},
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
  {%- if settings.email != blank %}
  "email": {{ settings.email | json }},
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if settings.founder_name != blank %}
  "founder": { "@type": "Person", "name": {{ settings.founder_name | json }} },
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if settings.phone != blank %}
  "contactPoint": {
    "@type": "ContactPoint",
    "contactType": "customer support",
    "telephone": {{ settings.phone | remove: ' ' | json }},
    {%- if settings.email != blank %}
    "email": {{ settings.email | json }},
    {%- endif %}
    "areaServed": "IN",
    "availableLanguage": ["en", "hi"]
  },
  {%- endif %}
  "address": {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    "addressLocality": "Raipur",
    "addressRegion": "Chhattisgarh",
    "addressCountry": "IN"
  }
}
</script>
